WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:05.810
So if Baron Zemo had to get a kidney transplant,
you would want him to change his name to has

00:00:05.810 --> 00:00:07.920
to go to the bathroom more often?

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:09.010
No.

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:13.400
Super powers are weird.

00:00:13.400 --> 00:00:16.450
Let's talk to Tom and Nina to answer this
question.

00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:19.410
What are the most useless superpowers in the
MCU?

00:00:19.410 --> 00:00:23.110
Nina, what are the most useless powers in
the MCU?

00:00:23.110 --> 00:00:28.650
So when you asked me to think about this question,
I knew my answer immediately, because I remember

00:00:28.650 --> 00:00:35.680
when I saw Guardians of the Galaxy 2 in theaters,
I took one look at Mantis and was like, "Why?"

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:42.780
And her super power being just a general vibe
check does not seem super useful to me.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:47.649
I don't know enough about kind of her comics
incarnation to know if she has some other

00:00:47.649 --> 00:00:52.440
good power, but I just did a rewatch of Infinity
War and End Game.

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:56.999
And when she's just on Thanos's head camping
out up there and is like, "He's mad."

00:00:56.999 --> 00:01:00.100
It's like, "Yeah, we know he's mad, Mantis.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:01.100
That's not helpful.

00:01:01.100 --> 00:01:02.640
Punch him or something."

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:07.329
So yeah, her energy reading thing is dumb.

00:01:07.329 --> 00:01:08.909
I don't like it.

00:01:08.909 --> 00:01:10.020
It's not a good superpower.

00:01:10.020 --> 00:01:11.020
But a fun character.

00:01:11.020 --> 00:01:12.020
That's my hot take.

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:13.020
Let's be real.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:14.460
She's a fun character and I like the actress.

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:19.719
It's just give her something else to do other
than be a super psychiatrist or whatever she's

00:01:19.719 --> 00:01:21.390
out there doing.

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:24.900
I don't see that being useful in any ... I
haven't seen it be useful yet and I don't

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:27.329
foresee a way in which it will ever be useful.

00:01:27.329 --> 00:01:30.541
Well, James Gunn is going to prove you wrong
in Guardians of the Galaxy -

00:01:30.541 --> 00:01:31.550
I hope he does.

00:01:31.550 --> 00:01:34.000
Again, I like the actress, I like the character.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.400
He's got to do something weird and cool, which
he's more than capable of doing.

00:01:37.400 --> 00:01:38.509
Have you seen Slither?

00:01:38.509 --> 00:01:41.640
I haven't, but I know I probably should.

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:42.640
Yeah, you should.

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:47.619
My pick for most useless superpower in the
MCU is Claw -

00:01:47.619 --> 00:01:48.619
Okay.

00:01:48.619 --> 00:01:55.259
- played by Andy Serkis in Avengers: Age of
Ultron and in Black Panther.

00:01:55.259 --> 00:02:05.149
So his deal is that he has a prosthetic arm
that can shoot concussive pulses, and that's

00:02:05.149 --> 00:02:07.130
pretty neat, I guess.

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:15.680
His hand got cut off by Ultron, And then he
got a robot arm and it shoots sound.

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:18.350
You know what might've been more useful?

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:20.900
I don't know, a gun, just a gun.

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:22.740
Just carry a gun.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:23.740
Right.

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:24.740
Your arm -

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:27.080
To use with your other arm, even.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:28.080
Right.

00:02:28.080 --> 00:02:35.180
It turns it ... it shoots sound waves, which
I guess is cool to talk about, but at the

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:39.820
end of the day, what about, I don't know,
a ballistic missile or -

00:02:39.820 --> 00:02:41.090
He figured out guns awhile ago.

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:42.840
They would do the trick.

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:43.840
- bullets.

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:44.840
Yeah.

00:02:44.840 --> 00:02:45.840
Yeah.

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:46.840
They're pretty effective.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:47.840
Yeah.

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:48.840
And let's also talk about this.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:49.950
I've known about this character for many,
many years.

00:02:49.950 --> 00:02:58.980
It doesn't make sense that his name is Claw,
does not have a hand, but it is not a claw.

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:01.000
His name is Claw.

00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:02.820
He should have at least one claw.

00:03:02.820 --> 00:03:06.600
So what you're saying is if somebody has a
defining feature about them, they should have

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:08.820
to change their name?

00:03:08.820 --> 00:03:11.932
I'm saying that if you are going to go out
of your way -

00:03:11.932 --> 00:03:14.270
If you're going to name him Claw, he should
have a claw.

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:20.830
He should have a claw, or at least be claw-like
in some way, like Dr. Claw from Inspector

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:21.830
Gadget.

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:22.830
That's exactly what I was thinking.

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:25.530
He doesn't have a claw, but that's okay.

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:26.530
He's evil-ish.

00:03:26.530 --> 00:03:27.530
It's fine.

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:30.160
This is a problematic worldview that you've
got right here, Brian.

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:31.160
He sucks.

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:32.160
Claw sucks.

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:34.500
He shows up in one movie, he's evil, he gets
his arm cut off.

00:03:34.500 --> 00:03:37.400
He shows up in the next movie, he gets killed
like a chump.

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:38.530
Claw, he sucks.

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:39.530
And his power sucks.

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:40.740
Use a gun.

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:46.330
So if Baron Zemo had to get a kidney transplant,
you would want him to change his name to has

00:03:46.330 --> 00:03:48.850
to go to the bathroom more often?

00:03:48.850 --> 00:03:56.630
No, I'm just saying that Claw is a fairly
menacing sounding name.

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:59.550
A claw is a weapon.

00:03:59.550 --> 00:04:00.770
What does he fight with?

00:04:00.770 --> 00:04:01.770
He fights with his claw.

00:04:01.770 --> 00:04:03.600
Not a claw, yeah.

00:04:03.600 --> 00:04:06.240
Wolverine fights with claws.

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:07.450
Claws are a thing.

00:04:07.450 --> 00:04:11.770
And he has nothing to do with Wolverine.

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:12.770
Nothing to do with Wolverine.

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:13.770
No.

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:14.770
Nothing to do with claws!

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:19.590
as a character without turning to narrative
crutches, like naming yourself after the thing

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:20.760
that's on your body.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:22.810
So you're pro Claw is what you're saying?

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:24.520
You like Ulysses Claw?

00:04:24.520 --> 00:04:25.520
Oh, I'm sorry, man.

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:26.520
Can we go back?

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:27.520
Can you reintroduce me?

00:04:27.520 --> 00:04:31.940
Instead of calling me Tom, could you just
call me skin tag he's trying to hide on camera

00:04:31.940 --> 00:04:32.940
right now.

00:04:32.940 --> 00:04:33.940
Oh my God.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:34.940
You need to pull your life together.

00:04:34.940 --> 00:04:37.000
You need to change your worldview.

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:38.000
Okay.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:39.900
So skin tag you're trying to hide on camera.

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:43.820
Please tell us, what are the most useless
superpowers in the MCU?

00:04:43.820 --> 00:04:45.000
I'm canceling you.

00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:50.120
First of all, Nina, I hate to disagree with
you, but Mantis is you can talk to, and I'm

00:04:50.120 --> 00:04:51.430
on board with that.

00:04:51.430 --> 00:04:55.169
That's basically all I've been looking for
my entire adult life.

00:04:55.169 --> 00:04:56.169
I don't think that Mantis is useless.

00:04:56.169 --> 00:04:59.610
Just a sensitive girl with a little ping pong
balls on her head?

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:05.230
Well, now that you put it that way, maybe
you've awakened something, but I'd rather

00:05:05.230 --> 00:05:06.610
shift topic.

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:08.680
Yeah, that's fine.

00:05:08.680 --> 00:05:11.340
I don't think that Mantis is useless.

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:17.560
Who I do think is useless is everybody else
in the MCU.

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:18.560
Roast battle.

00:05:18.560 --> 00:05:19.810
Nobody's safe.

00:05:19.810 --> 00:05:25.130
Starting out with Captain America, you took
human growth hormones from Germany and you

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:27.240
threw a garbage can lid at some people?

00:05:27.240 --> 00:05:31.790
Are you trying to be a superhero or my stepdad
Chip?

00:05:31.790 --> 00:05:32.950
Boom.

00:05:32.950 --> 00:05:37.300
Iron Man, I just rewatched your first couple
of movies.

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:41.340
Your power is that you pull the pads from
electronics to make a bulletproof suit that

00:05:41.340 --> 00:05:43.430
you wouldn't let the government take away
from you?

00:05:43.430 --> 00:05:44.510
Got bad news for you, man.

00:05:44.510 --> 00:05:45.510
You're not original.

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:46.889
I live above a methadone clinic.

00:05:46.889 --> 00:05:49.910
You're a dime a dozen.

00:05:49.910 --> 00:05:50.910
Boom.

00:05:50.910 --> 00:05:55.530
The Incredible Hulk, you got exposed to something
that makes you get angry and weirdly muscular.

00:05:55.530 --> 00:06:03.030
It's not gamma radiation, it's called the
Joe Rogan experience.

00:06:03.030 --> 00:06:06.260
Black Widow, you look like Scarlett Johannson
and I've had a crush on you since I went to

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:09.400
see Lost in Translation with my stepdad Chip.

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:14.419
What are you, my stepdad Chip?

00:06:14.419 --> 00:06:16.260
And finally, Hawkeye.

00:06:16.260 --> 00:06:19.990
Hawkeye, I appreciate that you found something
that was important to you and you've learned

00:06:19.990 --> 00:06:21.370
how to excel at it.

00:06:21.370 --> 00:06:25.270
I think that's really important, not to mention
the fact that you did it while supporting

00:06:25.270 --> 00:06:28.200
a family of three children and a lovely wife.

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:29.680
Good for you, man.

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:30.680
Two children.

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:32.120
You remind me of my stepdad Chip.

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:33.120
What?

00:06:33.120 --> 00:06:34.120
It's two children.

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:35.160
Didn't they have a third kid?

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:36.160
I don't think so.

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:38.570
I thought that was the whole thing, in Age
of Ultron.

00:06:38.570 --> 00:06:42.540
I hate to pull rank on you, man, but I think
that you are so wrong about that number.

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:43.669
I thought they had two kids?

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:45.980
Oh, was there another kid on the way?

00:06:45.980 --> 00:06:46.990
There was the third kid on the way.

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:52.169
And I think that they had to name it after
Aaron Taylor Johnson, because they felt bad.

00:06:52.169 --> 00:06:53.840
Oh, okay.

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:55.500
Oh, okay.

00:06:55.500 --> 00:06:57.169
Well, sorry.

00:06:57.169 --> 00:06:59.720
Sorry, I screwed up.

00:06:59.720 --> 00:07:05.010
So let me tell you briefly about porcupine
future telling lady.

00:07:05.010 --> 00:07:07.840
Wait, is this a real thing?

00:07:07.840 --> 00:07:10.449
Yes, this is a real thing.

00:07:10.449 --> 00:07:11.980
This is from Agents of Shield.

00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:14.520
Again, Agents of Shield.

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:15.520
Porcupine fortune telling lady in Agents of
Shield.

00:07:15.520 --> 00:07:17.540
Now it makes sense.

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:18.540
Okay.

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:19.630
Yeah, that checks out.

00:07:19.630 --> 00:07:24.080
So in Agents of Shield, there's this great
character played by Ruth Negga and she's great.

00:07:24.080 --> 00:07:25.490
Oh, I love Ruth Negga.

00:07:25.490 --> 00:07:31.730
Her name is Raina and I believe she's known
as the woman in the flower dress or something

00:07:31.730 --> 00:07:32.730
like that.

00:07:32.730 --> 00:07:33.730
Okay.

00:07:33.730 --> 00:07:34.730
Yeah.

00:07:34.730 --> 00:07:35.730
She's very manipulative and creepy and she's
after -

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:36.730
Oh, that's right.

00:07:36.730 --> 00:07:37.730
I forgot about her.

00:07:37.730 --> 00:07:41.760
- she's doing bad guy things, and that sets
up the Inhumans arc, where they're going to

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:45.449
go through Terrigenesis and she wants to go
through Terrigenesis so she can get her inhuman

00:07:45.449 --> 00:07:49.150
powers and be super powerful and be super
bad.

00:07:49.150 --> 00:07:56.449
And so she does, and she gets porcupine quills
all over her and she's really upset about

00:07:56.449 --> 00:07:57.449
it.

00:07:57.449 --> 00:07:58.449
As happens, yeah.

00:07:58.449 --> 00:08:02.080
Yeah, she's not into it at all.

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:03.240
That's also fair.

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:04.850
She's like, "This stinks."

00:08:04.850 --> 00:08:06.460
That's what she says.

00:08:06.460 --> 00:08:09.479
Direct quote, "This stinks."

00:08:09.479 --> 00:08:12.400
But eventually she learned she can also tell
the future.

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:16.270
So that happens, Inhumans.

00:08:16.270 --> 00:08:19.120
But there's no porcupine bite involved in
this.

00:08:19.120 --> 00:08:20.820
No, it's purely Terrigenesis.

00:08:20.820 --> 00:08:21.820
Wasted potential.

00:08:21.820 --> 00:08:28.610
She goes to Terrigenesis and she comes out
looking like a -

00:08:28.610 --> 00:08:29.610
Like a porcupine.

00:08:29.610 --> 00:08:30.610
Yeah.

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:31.610
Interesting.

00:08:31.610 --> 00:08:36.089
How do you feel about the Inhumans as a basis
for somebody getting super powers?

00:08:36.089 --> 00:08:40.570
I recognize that on paper, there's nothing
that makes it more or less ridiculous than

00:08:40.570 --> 00:08:43.919
being a mutant, but for some reason I just
never got on board with it.

00:08:43.919 --> 00:08:44.919
Yeah, I don't know.

00:08:44.919 --> 00:08:46.600
I think the Inhumans have potential.

00:08:46.600 --> 00:08:52.999
I think that there's fun to be had in the
Inhumans, but at the end of the day, I've

00:08:52.999 --> 00:08:54.950
been kind of hot and cold with them.

00:08:54.950 --> 00:08:58.860
I think that there's a lot of interesting
things that you could do with the Inhumans,

00:08:58.860 --> 00:09:03.019
but it's not my jam, as it were.

00:09:03.019 --> 00:09:09.129
Well, I mean to bring it back to what you
said at the beginning, or actually in a different

00:09:09.129 --> 00:09:13.860
episode, because time is a flat circle, I'm
sure nobody thought Guardians of the Galaxy

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:16.829
would ever be popular because it's really
weird.

00:09:16.829 --> 00:09:21.410
So I think with the right director and the
right cast, almost anything in Marvel, with

00:09:21.410 --> 00:09:29.329
some exceptions, could work on screen, but
you need the next kind of James Gunn type

00:09:29.329 --> 00:09:31.600
to really make it into something good.

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:36.319
So I think the Inhumans just needs a really
cracked director and cast if it's going to

00:09:36.319 --> 00:09:37.319
-

00:09:37.319 --> 00:09:41.069
Can we talk a bit about the Inhumans and some
of their useless powers?

00:09:41.069 --> 00:09:42.139
Could we?

00:09:42.139 --> 00:09:43.139
Black Bolt.

00:09:43.139 --> 00:09:44.139
Do you have feelings?

00:09:44.139 --> 00:09:45.279
How do you feel?

00:09:45.279 --> 00:09:48.589
How do I feel about Black Bolt?

00:09:48.589 --> 00:09:49.589
Yeah.

00:09:49.589 --> 00:09:52.910
Well, in general ... man, I got to say, I
don't know.

00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:57.589
It's just one of those subjective things where
... it's the same thing with magic in comics.

00:09:57.589 --> 00:10:00.529
Like I have the same problem with magic, like
Doctor Strange.

00:10:00.529 --> 00:10:04.029
I could never get into Doctor Strange because
the fact that he used magic always felt like

00:10:04.029 --> 00:10:05.029
a cheat code.

00:10:05.029 --> 00:10:08.970
It was always like, "Well, he can just magic
harder, and then he'll get out of the situation

00:10:08.970 --> 00:10:09.970
that he's in."

00:10:09.970 --> 00:10:14.439
But at the same time, everybody in Marvel,
everybody in comic books, they're all magic.

00:10:14.439 --> 00:10:15.439
It's just different.

00:10:15.439 --> 00:10:16.559
They just put different labels on it.

00:10:16.559 --> 00:10:20.699
Iron Man is technology magic, and Spider-Man
is sticky people magic.

00:10:20.699 --> 00:10:24.660
And everybody's a different kind of magic,
but for some reason it just doesn't click

00:10:24.660 --> 00:10:25.660
with me.

00:10:25.660 --> 00:10:27.339
And that's the thing with Inhumans.

00:10:27.339 --> 00:10:32.670
I mean, if there had been ... I don't know,
maybe it's just I never got into them when

00:10:32.670 --> 00:10:37.449
I was a kid, but Black Bolt, not any different
than an X-Man.

00:10:37.449 --> 00:10:40.880
There could be an X-Man who can't talk or
he'll explode a thing.

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:42.089
I like Black Bolt.

00:10:42.089 --> 00:10:43.439
I like looking at him.

00:10:43.439 --> 00:10:44.439
Sure.

00:10:44.439 --> 00:10:48.839
I think he's got a cool character design,
but Black Bolt's power is that every sound

00:10:48.839 --> 00:10:55.170
he makes is super-duper strong, super-duper
laughs so loud that it will disintegrate matter

00:10:55.170 --> 00:11:00.449
in front of him, so he doesn't talk.

00:11:00.449 --> 00:11:07.750
As a character, it's kind of hard to connect
when not only can they not say anything, they

00:11:07.750 --> 00:11:09.829
can't really even do anything.

00:11:09.829 --> 00:11:10.829
Right.

00:11:10.829 --> 00:11:18.980
So he just kind of stands around a lot and
gestures at people vaguely in the comics.

00:11:18.980 --> 00:11:19.980
See, I don't know.

00:11:19.980 --> 00:11:22.839
I feel like that could be ... cinematically,
that could be really fascinating.

00:11:22.839 --> 00:11:25.129
It could be interesting.

00:11:25.129 --> 00:11:28.750
Doug Jones made that movie Mute.

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:31.689
Really anytime ... if you could just get a
good actor behind it, then it kind of rocks.

00:11:31.689 --> 00:11:32.689
Yes.

00:11:32.689 --> 00:11:36.629
If you have somebody who can't talk and it
forces the audience to treat that character

00:11:36.629 --> 00:11:38.639
as a mirror, I think that could be fantastic.

00:11:38.639 --> 00:11:39.639
100%.

00:11:39.639 --> 00:11:43.189
Instead what they did was they had a cranky
guy when they made the -

00:11:43.189 --> 00:11:44.529
Inhuman show.

00:11:44.529 --> 00:11:45.879
IMAX, ABC.

00:11:45.879 --> 00:11:47.499
Yeah, the TV show.

00:11:47.499 --> 00:11:48.499
Right.

00:11:48.499 --> 00:11:49.499
Okay, but -

00:11:49.499 --> 00:11:53.499
It was just the guy who looked kind of vaguely
perturbed to have to be doing the show most

00:11:53.499 --> 00:11:54.499
of the time.

00:11:54.499 --> 00:11:55.829
That doesn't do anything.

00:11:55.829 --> 00:12:00.899
I agree with everything you're saying, but
his very power is so powerful that he can't

00:12:00.899 --> 00:12:02.829
even use it.

00:12:02.829 --> 00:12:03.829
That's the bit.

00:12:03.829 --> 00:12:04.829
I think that kind of rocks, man.

00:12:04.829 --> 00:12:06.089
I think that that's cool.

00:12:06.089 --> 00:12:10.329
I think it's the same thing that makes it
interesting when Superman holds back when

00:12:10.329 --> 00:12:11.329
he's fighting the bad guy.

00:12:11.329 --> 00:12:12.329
Yeah, but he still flies.

00:12:12.329 --> 00:12:14.639
The fact that he could explode everybody.

00:12:14.639 --> 00:12:15.639
Yeah, he does.

00:12:15.639 --> 00:12:16.639
Yeah.

00:12:16.639 --> 00:12:19.829
I'm saying he still flies, he still lifts
cars, he still will throw a punch, he'll still

00:12:19.829 --> 00:12:23.519
do a laser vision or a cold breath.

00:12:23.519 --> 00:12:28.139
Black Bolt just doesn't do anything.

00:12:28.139 --> 00:12:35.510
I want to like Black Bolt, but he's engineered
to not do things that you want to watch a

00:12:35.510 --> 00:12:38.110
super hero do, which is use their super powers.

00:12:38.110 --> 00:12:40.129
Okay, let's take this from a different angle
then.

00:12:40.129 --> 00:12:45.079
For the last 13 years we've been looking at
Marvel characters who all have the exact same

00:12:45.079 --> 00:12:48.189
traits, namely they're overconfident and they
talk too much.

00:12:48.189 --> 00:12:51.790
This could be a huge change in tone for the
entire franchise, to just have one character

00:12:51.790 --> 00:12:54.029
who shuts the hell up the whole time.

00:12:54.029 --> 00:12:55.709
I'm not against that.

00:12:55.709 --> 00:12:59.100
You want a quieter, more introspective approach
to them.

00:12:59.100 --> 00:13:00.100
Yeah.

00:13:00.100 --> 00:13:02.929
I think that could be the most progressive
movement that the MCU has ever made is to

00:13:02.929 --> 00:13:06.209
introduce a white character who does not talk.

00:13:06.209 --> 00:13:07.550
Wow.

00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:08.550
That would be very different.

00:13:08.550 --> 00:13:11.370
Just sits on his throne not talking.

00:13:11.370 --> 00:13:14.759
Just shut up, yeah.

00:13:14.759 --> 00:13:16.459
All right.

00:13:16.459 --> 00:13:17.459
Thanks for joining us.

00:13:17.459 --> 00:13:20.579
Please hit like and subscribe so you don't
miss a single episode.

